==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zory|Zories]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~30 seconds<sup>400f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zir Zeal]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 40~53.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Le'boin]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 73.33~113.33 seconds<sup>2,200f~3,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Kang Roo]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 43.33~80 seconds<sup>1,300f~2,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Mooth]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The non-[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] peons do almost no damage, so you can just let them damage the [[Cat Base]] for a while. Once you kill one or two of them, the main threats start to appear. The only one to really worry about is Zir Zeal as he can burrow under your main force. If you've beaten Chapter 3, keep [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] off cooldown to deal with the Zir Zeal's 1,500 range burrow.

If you take too long, Mooth and Kang Roo will spawn. They honestly aren't much of a hassle, just get to the base before then and you'll be fine. Like usual, [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cat]] spam is always a good idea since there is no boss shockwave.

